  "$comment": "Refurbished's kitchen drawer, front to -z here (its facing names its back). The block is swapped for body (the counter with the openings of its two drawers), tray (the upper drawer) and tray_lower (the lower one, which Refurbished draws as a fixed panel), each a box you can look into, Refurbished's own boxes and textures turned round; code slides each 11 pixels out on its own. A click on a drawer's front pulls it out or pushes it in. Items lie anywhere on each drawer's floor, up to its back wall (surface 0 the upper, 1 the lower), written where the open drawer has them (code moves them with it and hides those of a shut drawer). The camera faces the drawers from the front, steeply from above so a drawer's floor shows; code takes it along with the drawer pulled out, over the middle of its floor. The upper drawer's floor (tray_floor, a hit box only) stops the cursor: pulled out, the drawer covers the lower one's front, which cannot be clicked through it; a click on it does nothing.",
